<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 25 February, from 138 to 1986.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/antoninus-pius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antoninus-pius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">138 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,888 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hadrian adopts Antoninus Pius as his heir</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hadrian made Antoninus his successor on condition that he adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-aurelius">Marcus Aurelius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-verus">Lucius Verus</a>. The arrangement secured more than four decades of stable rule.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/628">628 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,398 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kavad II overthrows his father Khosrow II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kavad-ii">Kavad II</a> overthrew his father, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a>, the last great king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, after the defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a>, and had him killed. Kavad made peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> but died within the year, starting a succession crisis.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kavad-ii">Kavad II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1570">1570 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">456 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Pius V excommunicates Elizabeth I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Regnans in Excelsis declared Elizabeth a heretic and released her subjects from obedience. English Catholics came to be seen as potential traitors, and persecution intensified.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1705">1705 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">321 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Handel's opera Nero opens in Hamburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-frideric-handel">George Frideric Handel</a>'s opera <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> opened in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a>, with Mattheson in the title role. Less successful than his Almira, it ran for only three performances before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> closed for Lent, and its music has not survived.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-frideric-handel">George Frideric Handel</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1836">1836 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">190 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samuel Colt patents his revolver</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colt received a US patent for a revolving-cylinder pistol. His first company failed, but orders during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war">Mexican-American War</a> made Colt revolvers famous worldwide.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1870">1870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hiram Revels becomes the first African American US Senator</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> minister was sworn in after a fierce debate over his eligibility. He filled the seat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jefferson-davis">Jefferson Davis</a> had left when the South seceded.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1932">1932 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">94 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Adolf Hitler acquires German citizenship</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stateless since renouncing his Austrian citizenship in 1925, Hitler was given a nominal post in the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, making him a German citizen. He could now stand for President.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1986">1986 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">40 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">People Power Revolution forces Marcos from the Philippines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After days of peaceful mass protest, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-marcos">Ferdinand Marcos</a> fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corazon-aquino">Corazon Aquino</a> was sworn in as president. His two decades of rule had included years of martial law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li></ol>
